// A static property (self::$made = ..., C::$made++) and a variable variable
// ($$name = e, ${expr} = e) are assignable heads too. A static head carries its base
// and property name, a variable-variable head the THUNK that computes the name, and
// every reader below asks refNameV for the name - so one code path serves all three.
// The static form must be tried FIRST or PlainHead never sees it.
TargetHead  = StaticHead | GlobalsHead | PlainHead | VarVarHead ;
