    // -why. This is the same marker every other handle-IR language emits, but it
    // cannot be core stmtPos (lib/compile-core.js): up.pos is the position AFTER the
    // tag's node matched, and PHP's whitespace INCLUDES newlines and comments, so
    // a statement's node ends past every blank and comment line that follows its
    // ';' - the last statement of a file would be attributed past EOF. The
    // Statement rule therefore captures the position of the statement's FIRST
    // token (an empty token skips whitespace before matching, so it lands on the
    // token itself) and hands over [pos, thunk].
